Example 1.3 Suppose the demand is distributed according to an exponential distribution with mean \(\theta\). Find the optimal action.







NoteSolution





Recall that the CDF of the exponential distribution with mean \(\theta\) is given by \[
  F(w) = 1 - e^{-w/\theta}.
\] Since \(F\) is continuous and strictly increasing, the optimal action is the unique \(a\) such that \(F(a) = 1 - p/q\). \[
  F(a) = 1 - p/q
  \iff
  e^{-a/\theta} = p/q
  \iff
  -a/\theta = \ln(p/q)
  \iff
  a = -\theta \ln(p/q) = \theta \ln \frac{q}{p}.
\]





1.3.2 Back to discrete version
