Proposition 7.1 (Dynamic programming) Define the following value functions \(V^*_t \colon \S \to \reals\) \[V^*_{T+1}(s) = 0\] and for \(t \in \{T, \dots, 1\}\) \[ Q^*_t(s, a) = p a + \EXP[ h(s + a - W_t) + V^*_{t+1}( s + a - W_t ) ]\] and \[ \begin{align*}
  V^*_t(s) &= \min_{a \in \S_{\ge 0}} Q^*_t(s,a) \\
  π^*_t(s) &= \arg \min_{a \in \S_{\ge 0}} Q^*_t(s,a)
  \end{align*}
\] Then the strategy \(π^* = (π^*_1, \dots, π^*_T)\) is optimal.








